<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>LetsDANE - Security Dashboard</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div>
    <h1>🔒 LetsDANE</h1>
    <p>DNSSEC · Handshake · DANE security manager</p>
  </div>
  <span id="overall-status" class="badge">Running</span>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="cards">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Proxy</h2>
      <strong id="proxy-status">Loading</strong>
      <p id="proxy-address">127.0.0.1:8080</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Local CA</h2>
      <strong id="ca-status">Loading</strong>
      <p>Private key stored locally</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Certificate downloads</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Import the PEM certificate into Firefox or Brave as a trusted root.
      Both browsers use the same PEM file.
    </p>
    <div class="downloads">
      <a class="download-btn primary-download" href="/api/ca/cert.pem" download>
        <strong>.crt — for Firefox</strong>
        <span>PEM X.509, filename letsdane-ca.crt</span>
        <em>Download</em>
      </a>
      <a class="download-btn" href="/api/ca/cert.der" download>
        <strong>.der — for Android / system</strong>
        <span>DER X.509, filename letsdane-ca.der</span>
        <em>Download</em>
      </a>
      <a class="download-btn" href="/api/ca/ca.pem" download="ca.pem">
        <strong>.pem — for Brave</strong>
        <span>PEM X.509, filename ca.pem</span>
        <em>Download</em>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>DNS Trust &amp; Resolvers</h2>
    <p class="muted">Configure your Handshake-aware DNS resolver.</p>

    <label for="primary">Primary resolver (IPv4 or IPv6)</label>
    <input id="primary" autocomplete="off" placeholder="82.68.70.162 or 2001:db8::1">
    <div class="test-row">
      <button id="test-primary">Test primary</button>
      <span id="primary-result" class="result"></span>
    </div>

    <label for="secondary">Secondary resolver (IPv4 or IPv6, optional)</label>
    <input id="secondary" autocomplete="off" placeholder="82.68.70.163">
    <div class="toggle">
      <input type="checkbox" id="useSecondary">
      <label for="useSecondary">Enable secondary resolver (failover)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="test-row">
      <button id="test-secondary">Test secondary</button>
      <span id="secondary-result" class="result"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="active-info">
      Active resolver: <strong id="active-resolver">Not selected</strong>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>ICANN TLDs</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      TLDs listed here resolve through the normal OS/ICANN DNS.
      All other names (including Handshake names) use the configured HNS resolver.
      Adding or removing a TLD takes effect <strong>immediately</strong> —
      no restart required.
    </p>

    <div class="tld-add-row">
      <input id="icann-tld" placeholder="com" autocomplete="off">
      <button id="add-tld">Add TLD</button>
    </div>
    
    <div class="tld-bulk-row">
      <label for="bulk-tld-file" class="bulk-label">Bulk upload (CSV or one-per-line)</label>
      <input id="bulk-tld-file" type="file" accept=".csv,.txt">
      <button id="bulk-tld-apply">Import</button>
      <span id="bulk-tld-result" class="result"></span>
    </div>
<div id="tld-error" class="result failure"></div>

    <h3>Configured ICANN TLDs <span id="tld-count" class="muted"></span></h3>
    <div id="icann-tld-list" class="tld-chips"></div>

    <button id="save-settings" class="primary">Save trust configuration</button>
    <p id="trust-save-result" class="result"></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Security policy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>ICANN TLDs: OS/ICANN resolver, standard CA validation</li>
      <li>All other namespaces (HNS): configured resolver</li>
      <li>DANE TLSA: mandatory when TLSA present (usage 3 / DANE-Ee)</li>
      <li>Certificate mismatch: connection blocked</li>
      <li>No TLSA on ICANN name: standard CA validation</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>CA details</h2>
    <dl id="ca-info"></dl>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Installation</h2>
    <a href="/install.html">Firefox / Brave installation guide</a>
  </section>
</main>

<footer>LetsDANE JS · Local dashboard</footer>
<script src="/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
